{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/cnn/posts/flags-with-blue-lines-have-been-closely-associated-with-the-blue-lives-matter-mo/10160083307241509/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/cnn/posts/flags-with-blue-lines-have-been-closely-associated-with-the-blue-lives-matter-mo/10160083307241509/","title":"CNN","description":"Flags with blue lines have been closely associated with the Blue Lives Matter movement, a national organization formed largely as a response to the Black Lives Matter movement","language":"en","text":"Flags with blue lines have been closely associated with the Blue Lives Matter movement, a national organization formed largely as a response to the Black Lives Matter movement\n\nAll reactions:\n\n1.3K comments\n\n171 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nNathan Hill\n\nFact of the matter is that this defaces the American flag. Plain and simple. As do shirts, ties, shorts, dresses, shoes and any other apparel.\n\nAmanda Myers\n\nSmart of the police department to not put this up. Terrible optics. It's not an official American flag, and it's too easy for people to see it as more of an \"anti black lives matter\" symbol. I have friends in MD who like Hogan, but he needs to stay out of the fray on this.\n\nAshley Nichole\n\nI'm super confused as to why the governor thinks that HIS personal views should dictate whether or not law enforcement personnel display this flag, when the entire discussion is centered around those personnel and has zero to do the governor. Stay in your lane, perhaps\n\n18\n\nEddie Ferrell\n\nNo one cared until the black lives matter movement came out of course it's dismissive.\n\nPeople are so ignorant.\n\nJudy Talley\n\nI think the best flag would be multi-colored, symbolizing that ALL lives matter.\n\nDouglas Fleury\n\nAnd they’re right. The problem with the “blue lives matter” flag is that a lot of people use it as an “anti black lives matter” symbol.\n\n32\n\nView all 3 replies\n\nLa'Trice Lott\n\nThe same faux patriots that pitch a fit about how disrespectful it is to kneel for the anthem or not stand for the pledge of allegiance, have no problem with the flag being altered. That folks, is hypocrisy at it's finest.\n\n25\n\nView all 10 replies\n\nJennifer Sellmeyer Maxey\n\nThat Thin Blue Line represents respect, grieving, sorrow, love.. for someone that lost their life in the line of duty.\n\n49\n\nView all 20 replies\n\nTom DeGraffenreid\n\nFirst, PD cannot accept gifts from the public. Second, it certainly can’t display them, as it is terrible optics for a department to do so, since it can be construed as implicit bias toward one member of the community over another- and don’t think for a second it wouldn’t come into play down the road.\n\n127\n\nView all 32 replies\n\nDavid Pagnier\n\nI agree with the premise that it is not an American flag and cant replace one. The whole idea of that flag was to nullify black lives matter more than honoring popo.\n\n76\n\nView all 12 replies","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2321.0718109912705,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}